Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:54:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 27/29] metal: profile-driven speedups, 19.3s -> 6.8s on LWA
 4-slot dirty

Bottleneck map (was: 4.5s Metal grid + 4.7s CPU FFT/roll/extract + ~10s
serial host prep, all repeated 12x by fixed 1M-item chunks):
- adaptive row chunks from a 2 GB/item-data budget (12M items): 1 chunk
  for the 4-slot case, 201 planes processed once not 967x (4.8x less FFT).
- parallel item pass (split+wrap+sincos+wphase+plane, GCD, per-index
  writes) with cached split reused across the ~7 gatherings per item.
- parallel plane gather (GCD, per-plane slots, serial compact in order).
- parallel two-phase extract+screens (conflict-free row sets).
- shared compute grid buffer with GPU blit fill/copy (no 2 GB memset).
- phase timers (MX_METAL_DEBUG_TIMING chunk phases).
All bit-preserving (1-vis 2.95e-07, lwa50k 1.45e-08, T2 dirty 4.8e-06).
Remaining: Metal grid 2.7s + other 2.5s; band-limited FFTs are next.

